    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE <Layout>
         breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with the misleading "unable to find matching
         parent xml file" error.

         2026-08-10 (code review 3B/3C, C1 half 1) - Disposition__c ADDED. ONE layoutItem. No
         field was moved, removed or re-ordered, and no section, button or related list changed.

         🔴 WHY THIS IS NOT COSMETIC. 3C gave Contract_Review__c an Acquisition_PSA /
         Disposition_PSA record-type pair, a Disposition__c lookup, two Paths, a record-type
         gate split in RecordStageAdvanceService, two sharing rules and an entire
         ContractExecutionService disposition arm - and the lookup that DECIDES which arm runs
         appeared on NO layout. Contract_Review_Record_Page renders force:detailPanel, which IS
         this layout, so before this edit nobody - administrator included - had a field to set.

         🔴 THIS LOOKUP IS THE ROUTING SWITCH, NOT A LABEL. ContractExecutionService.handleExecution
         runs BOTH arms unconditionally through two independent ifs: Opportunity__c drives the
         acquisition handoff, Disposition__c moves the sale to Closing. A row with neither
         populated executes and does nothing at all, silently - which is exactly the state every
         hand-created disposition PSA was in before this edit.

         ⚠ THIS FILE ALONE DOES NOT MAKE A DISPOSITION PSA CREATABLE. It makes the parent
         SETTABLE and VISIBLE once a row exists. Creation is D15/Q3 + D16.2 auto-create on entry
         to the Disposition_Stage__c = 'PSA' stage, which is Apex (DispositionStageEntryService)
         and is owned by the developer half of this fix. The Contract Review related list on
         Disposition_Record_Page is the second half and is in this same change.

         ⚠ Opportunity__c IS ALSO ON THIS LAYOUT AS Edit, AND THAT MATTERS MORE HERE THAN IT
         LOOKS. D23 grants the disposition personas Opportunity__c as READ-ONLY at the FLS level
         precisely because its blank is load-bearing - an editable grant would let a disposition
         persona populate it and mint a phantom acquisition Transaction__c. Layout behavior is
         not a permission: FLS wins, so the field renders read-only for those personas
         regardless of the Edit behavior recorded here. Do not "fix" the layout behavior to match
         - one layout serves both record types and the acquisition persona legitimately edits it.

         ⚠ ONE LAYOUT SERVES BOTH RECORD TYPES (design S3 / gate T-A3 asks for a separate
         disposition layout; per-record-type layout ASSIGNMENT is profile-only and profiles/** is
         .forceignore'd here, so that half is a post-deploy gate - D15 finding #5). The lookup is
         therefore also visible on an acquisition PSA, where it is correctly blank.

         PLACED IMMEDIATELY AFTER Opportunity__c ON PURPOSE - the two parent lookups are mutually
         exclusive by construction, and a reader must be able to see which one is populated.
    -->
